<item>
            <title>[LU-20251] osd-wbcfs doesn&apos;t handle dentry pinning correctly on newer kernels</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20251</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Swapping kill_litter_super() to kill_anon_super() removes the implicit d_genocide() that cleans up stale dentry during umount. This causes warnings and hangs during umount. Refactor osd-wbcfs to handle these changes better.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
